@startuml state-book-copy
title BookCopy - State Diagram (CopyStatus)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #444444
}

' States are exactly the CopyStatus enum values from the glossary.
' Each transition label: trigger [requirement] / guard.

[*] --> AVAILABLE : add copy [FR-03]

state AVAILABLE
state ON_LOAN
state ON_HOLD
state LOST
state DAMAGED
state WITHDRAWN

AVAILABLE --> ON_LOAN : checkout [FR-13, FR-14]

ON_LOAN --> AVAILABLE : return, no reservation waiting [FR-17]
ON_LOAN --> ON_HOLD : return, reservation waiting [FR-17, FR-23]
ON_LOAN --> LOST : mark lost [FR-20]

ON_HOLD --> ON_LOAN : checkout to member of READY reservation [FR-26]
ON_HOLD --> ON_HOLD : hold expired, next WAITING reservation [FR-24]
ON_HOLD --> AVAILABLE : hold expired or cancelled, queue empty [FR-24, FR-25]

AVAILABLE --> DAMAGED : librarian sets status [FR-04]
AVAILABLE --> LOST : librarian sets status [FR-04]
AVAILABLE --> WITHDRAWN : librarian sets status [FR-04]

DAMAGED --> AVAILABLE : librarian restores [FR-04]
LOST --> AVAILABLE : librarian restores (copy found) [FR-04]
WITHDRAWN --> AVAILABLE : librarian restores [FR-04]

note right of AVAILABLE
  Counted in Title.availableCopyCount() (FR-05).
  Only state from which checkout is allowed (FR-13).
end note

note bottom of ON_LOAN
  Exactly one active Loan (ACTIVE or OVERDUE)
  references the copy (NFR-03).
  FR-04 changes are refused in ON_LOAN and ON_HOLD.
end note

note bottom of ON_HOLD
  Exactly one READY Reservation holds the copy.
  Only that member may borrow it (FR-26).
end note

note bottom of DAMAGED
  DAMAGED, LOST and WITHDRAWN may also be changed
  to one another by the librarian [FR-04].
  None of them can be lent or held.
end note

@enduml
